# 26. 500 — Internal Server Error

Remember:

```text
500 → Unexpected server/application failure
```

Check:

```text
Exception
Stack trace
Logs
Middleware
Database
Service layer
```

---

# 27. Check Exception

Suppose API returns:

```text
500 Internal Server Error
```

Don't stop there.

Run the API in Visual Studio and inspect:

```text
Exception
Message
Stack Trace
Inner Exception
Source
Line Number
```

Example:

```text
NullReferenceException
   at EmployeeService.GetEmployee(...)
   at EmployeesController.GetEmployee(...)
```

Now you know the problem is probably around the service operation.

---

# 28. Check Stack Trace

Suppose:

```text
Controller
   ↓
Service
   ↓
Repository
   ↓
SQL
```

Exception:

```text
SqlException
   ↓
EmployeeRepository.GetByIdAsync()
   ↓
EmployeeService.GetByIdAsync()
   ↓
EmployeesController.GetById()
```

The repository/database layer becomes the main area to investigate.

---

# 29. Check Logs

Use:

```csharp
_logger.LogError(
    ex,
    "Error while retrieving employee {EmployeeId}",
    id);
```

A useful log should tell you:

```text
What operation failed?
Which entity/request?
What exception occurred?
```

Avoid logging passwords, access tokens, connection-string secrets, or other sensitive information.

---

# 30. Check Middleware

A global exception middleware can catch unhandled exceptions and provide consistent responses.

Example:

```csharp
public class GlobalExceptionMiddleware
{
    private readonly RequestDelegate _next;
    private readonly ILogger<GlobalExceptionMiddleware> _logger;

    public GlobalExceptionMiddleware(
        RequestDelegate next,
        ILogger<GlobalExceptionMiddleware> logger)
    {
        _next = next;
        _logger = logger;
    }

    public async Task InvokeAsync(HttpContext context)
    {
        try
        {
            await _next(context);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Unhandled exception");

            context.Response.StatusCode = 500;
            context.Response.ContentType = "application/json";

            await context.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new
            {
                message = "An unexpected error occurred."
            });
        }
    }
}
```

Register it early enough in the pipeline to catch exceptions from downstream middleware/endpoints:

```csharp
app.UseMiddleware<GlobalExceptionMiddleware>();
```

---

# 31. Check Service Layer

Suppose:

```csharp
public async Task<EmployeeResponseDto?> GetByIdAsync(int id)
{
    var employee = await _repository.GetByIdAsync(id);

    return new EmployeeResponseDto
    {
        EmployeeId = employee.EmployeeId,
        Name = employee.Name
    };
}
```

If:

```text
employee == null
```

then:

```text
employee.EmployeeId
```

can cause:

```text
NullReferenceException
```

Safer:

```csharp
if (employee == null)
{
    return null;
}
```

Then the controller can return:

```csharp
return NotFound();
```

instead of allowing an unexpected exception to become a 500.

---

# 32. Check Database Layer

If the repository fails, check:

```text
Connection
SQL command
Parameters
Stored procedure
Table
Column names
Data types
Constraints
Transaction
```

Example:

```csharp
command.Parameters.Add(
    new SqlParameter("@EmployeeId", employeeId));
```

Make sure the parameter matches the SQL:

```sql
WHERE EmployeeId = @EmployeeId
```

