# 35. Real-World Troubleshooting Method

When you get an error, follow **five steps**.

## Step 1 — Reproduce

Can you consistently reproduce the problem?

```text
GET /api/employees/10
```

---

## Step 2 — Identify the Layer

```text
HTTP
 ↓
Middleware
 ↓
Controller
 ↓
Service
 ↓
Repository
 ↓
Database
```

Find where it fails.

---

## Step 3 — Inspect

Use:

```text
Swagger
Postman
Browser DevTools
Visual Studio Debugger
Logs
SQL Server
```

---

## Step 4 — Fix Root Cause

Don't simply hide the error.

For example, don't turn every exception into:

```text
return Ok();
```

Instead, fix the underlying problem.

---

## Step 5 — Retest

After fixing:

```text
Unit Test
   ↓
API Test
   ↓
Integration Test
   ↓
Git Commit
   ↓
CI Pipeline
```

